{"tool_name":"sugarcane_genome_hub","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"Sugarcane_Genome_Hub","home":"https://sugarcane-genome.cirad.fr/","license":"GPL-2.0","summary":"The Sugarcane Genome Hub is an integrated web-based database providing centralized access to the sugarcane reference genome sequences and genomic resources.","addition_date":"2019-12-11T16:03:11Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:59:41.392523Z","tool_type":["Database portal"],"collections":["Genome Hub","elixir-fr-sdp-2019"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:Sugarcane_Genome_Hub","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"droc@cirad.fr","name":"Gaetan Droc","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1849-1269","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]},{"email":"olivier.garsmeur@cirad.fr","name":"Olivier Garsmeur","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8869-3689","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"name":"CIRAD","typeEntity":"Institute"}],"documentation":[{"type":["Terms of use"],"url":"https://sugarcane-genome.cirad.fr/content/terms-service"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["gdroc"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Database search results","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2080"}},{"data":{"term":"Keyword","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0968"}},{"data":{"term":"Sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2044"}}],"operation":[{"term":"Sequence annotation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0361"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2044"}},{"data":{"term":"Sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0863"}}]}],"maturity":"Emerging","name":"Sugarcane Genome Hub","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"mrouard","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/s41467-018-05051-5","metadata":{"abstract":"Sugarcane (Saccharum spp.) is a major crop for sugar and bioenergy production. Its highly polyploid, aneuploid, heterozygous, and interspecific genome poses major challenges for producing a reference sequence. We exploited colinearity with sorghum to produce a BAC-based monoploid genome sequence of sugarcane. A minimum tiling path of 4660 sugarcane BAC that best covers the gene-rich part of the sorghum genome was selected based on whole-genome profiling, sequenced, and assembled in a 382-Mb single tiling path of a high-quality sequence. A total of 25,316 protein-coding gene models are predicted, 17% of which display no colinearity with their sorghum orthologs. We show that the two species, S. officinarum and S. spontaneum, involved in modern cultivars differ by their transposable elements and by a few large chromosomal rearrangements, explaining their distinct genome size and distinct basic chromosome numbers while also suggesting that polyploidization arose in both lineages after their divergence.","authors":[{"name":"Aitken K."},{"name":"Antonise R."},{"name":"Berges H."},{"name":"Chan A."},{"name":"Charron C."},{"name":"Cherukuri Y."},{"name":"Costet L."},{"name":"D'Hont A."},{"name":"Droc G."},{"name":"Garsmeur O."},{"name":"Glaszmann J.C."},{"name":"Grimwood J."},{"name":"Healey A."},{"name":"Henry R."},{"name":"Hervouet C."},{"name":"Jenkins J."},{"name":"Kilian A."},{"name":"Martin G."},{"name":"Potier B."},{"name":"Schmutz J."},{"name":"Simmons B."},{"name":"Sims D."},{"name":"Sreedasyam A."},{"name":"Swaminathan K."},{"name":"Town C."},{"name":"Van Der Vossen E."},{"name":"Van Sluys M.-A."},{"name":"Yahiaoui N."}],"citationCount":295,"date":"2018-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Communications","title":"A mosaic monoploid reference sequence for the highly complex genome of sugarcane"},"pmcid":"PMC6035169","pmid":"29980662"}],"topic":[{"term":"Agricultural science","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3810"},{"term":"Bioinformatics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0091"},{"term":"Genomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0622"},{"term":"Model organisms","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_